<prov:Activity rdf:about="http://www.semanticweb.org/swo_prov#GenerationActivity">
  <rdfs:label>Ontology generation by OntoGeneration Agent (step 3)</rdfs:label>
  <prov:used rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/swo_prov#CandidateTerms"/>
  <prov:used rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/swo_prov#ProposedAxioms"/>
  <prov:used rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/swo_prov#ProposedTests"/>
  <prov:generated rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/swo#"/>
  <prov:wasInformedBy rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/swo_prov#TestGenerationActivity"/>
  <prov:wasAssociatedWith rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/swo_prov#agent_OntoGeneration_Agent"/>
  <prov:hadRole rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/swo_prov#GeneratorRole"/>
  <prov:hadPlan rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/swo_prov#GenerationPrompt"/>
  <prov:qualifiedAssociation>
    <prov:Association>
      <prov:agent rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/swo_prov#agent_OntoGeneration_Agent"/>
      <prov:hadRole rdf:resource="http://www.semanticweb.org/swo_prov#GeneratorRole"/>
    </prov:Association>
  </prov:qualifiedAssociation>
  <vaem:rationale>The ontology models all supplied classes, properties, and individuals to answer each competency question directly. Classes are organized under their explicit superclasses (Software, DataFormat). Sibling classes are declared disjoint. Properties carry the exact domains and ranges from the proposed axioms, with a coined general property hasFormat unifying inputFormat and outputFormat. Datatype properties use the specified XSD types. Individuals are typed according to their contextual class. Every entity lists its serving competency questions and design rationale.</vaem:rationale>
</prov:Activity>

